PLR 8.3: after a completed (no-match) loop over a non-empty
sequence the loop variable holds the LAST element -- the scan's
else-arm now binds the row index to len-1 (exact: equals
xs[len-1] AND inherits the no-match forall), with the empty-source
case carried by the path-sensitive $bound machinery
(UnboundLocalError at a post-loop read, as in CPython).
